.TH "git-squash" 1 "March 2018" "git-squash 0.1.0" "git-squash - squash all commits ahead of the upstream branch"

.SH NAME
git-squash - squash all commits ahead of the upstream branch

.SH SYNOPSIS
git squash [<upstream>]

.SH DESCRIPTION
git\-squash \- squash all commits ahead of the merge base with <upstream> into a
single commit. These are the commits that would be available for change in git
rebase --keep-base -i.

When <upstream> is omitted, use the tracked upstream branch if there is one,
otherwise the default branch.

Refuses to run with uncommitted changes. Resets to the merge base with
--soft, then opens an editor with the messages of all squashed commits. Lines
starting with # are removed from the message. If the commit fails or is
aborted, the branch is restored to its original state.

Works for branches that contain merges because it does not use rebase.
